    {
      "id": "MR-C58-ekonis",
      "sequence": 2380,
      "title": "एकोणीस (ekoṇīs) — nineteen",
      "headword": "एकोणीस",
      "romanization": "ekoṇīs",
      "gloss": "nineteen — one LESS than twenty, which is why it is taught after twenty and not before",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:786305201c0d1a96",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Count from एक to अठरा (aṭhrā) and stop. The book has taken you no further than that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: एकोणीस",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "एकोणीस — ekoṇīs — 19."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This one breaks the pattern on purpose, and it is why वीस (vīs) came first: you cannot build nineteen until you have twenty. एकोणीस (ekoṇīs) is एक (one) plus ऊन (less) plus वीस (vīs) (twenty): one less than twenty, counting DOWN from the round number rather than up from the ten."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin does the same thing with undeviginti, and so does the clock face when somebody says quarter to. Marathi uses this एकोण- trick at every nineteen — twenty-nine, thirty-nine and the rest are all built this way — so learning it once buys every one of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
